  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of the wife giving a look",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the wife gives a disapproving look, as indicated by the text 'and your wife gives you this look'. The deictic 'your' directly implicates the viewer as the recipient of the wife's look, making the user the subject of the wife's reaction. The user is also implicitly projected onto the textual description of returning from suicide bombing, as the text 'when you come home from a long day of suicide bombin' uses 'you' to address the viewer as the person performing the action. The visual material of the woman's expression is mapped onto this textual description, creating a unified projection where the user is the central figure in both the textual and visual narrative.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
